From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - fail a request whose response the mailbox reports as bad

spu_rx_callback() ignores mssg->error. The FlexRM mailbox sets it for
every response, -EIO among others when the ring is shut down, and the
PDC mailbox now sets -EIO for a receive overflow. The callback then
reads the status word of a response that did not arrive, and can
complete the request as good.

Complete the request with the error from the mailbox.

A response without a request context also jumped to finish_req(), which
dereferences the context. Just return: there is no request to complete.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -1658,10 +1658,13 @@ static void spu_rx_callback(struct mbox_client *cl, void *msg)
 	if (unlikely(!rctx)) {
 		/* This is fatal */
 		pr_err("%s(): no request context", __func__);
-		err = -EFAULT;
-		goto cb_finish;
+		return;
 	}
 
+	err = mssg->error;
+	if (unlikely(err))
+		goto cb_finish;
+
 	/* process the SPU status */
 	err = spu->spu_status_process(rctx->msg_buf.rx_stat);
 	if (err != 0) {
